### Available strategies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/strategies

### Equal weight, no constraints (feasible)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbols": ["AAPL", "MSFT", "VOO", "BND", "GLD"],
  "strategy": "equal-weight",
  "riskFreeRate": 0.04
}

> {%
    client.test("Equal weights", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected HTTP 200");
        client.assert(response.body.allocations.every(a => Math.abs(a.weight - 0.2) < 1e-9), "Every weight should be 0.2");
        client.assert(response.body.feasible === true, "No constraints, so it must be feasible");
    });
%}

### Equal weight with constraints it breaks (feasible = false, violations listed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbols": ["AAPL", "MSFT", "VOO", "BND", "GLD"],
  "strategy": "equal-weight",
  "riskFreeRate": 0.04,
  "constraints": [
    { "type": "ASSET_WEIGHT_BOUNDS", "symbol": "AAPL", "min": 0, "max": 0.1 },
    { "type": "SECTOR_LIMIT", "sector": "Technology", "maxWeight": 0.3 },
    { "type": "MAX_ASSETS", "count": 3 },
    { "type": "MIN_EXPECTED_RETURN", "value": 0.5 }
  ]
}

### Unknown strategy (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbols": ["AAPL", "VOO"],
  "strategy": "magic"
}

### Impossible bounds: 5 assets with at most 10% each (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbols": ["AAPL", "MSFT", "VOO", "BND", "GLD"],
  "strategy": "equal-weight",
  "constraints": [
    { "type": "WEIGHT_BOUNDS", "min": 0, "max": 0.1 }
  ]
}

### Invalid constraint: min greater than max (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbols": ["AAPL", "VOO"],
  "strategy": "equal-weight",
  "constraints": [
    { "type": "WEIGHT_BOUNDS", "min": 0.8, "max": 0.2 }
  ]
}

### Missing fields (expect 400 with field errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/optimization/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbols": [],
  "strategy": ""
}
